.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-BLUEGREEN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-bluegreen
.Nd blue/green changes for one workload, or for a whole cluster
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | rollback
.Nm
.Cm preview | cutover
.Ar track
.Nm
.Cm cluster
.Cm status
.Nm
.Cm cluster
.Cm deploy
.Ar track
.Op Ar kube-cluster-options ...
.Nm
.Cm cluster
.Cm promote | destroy
.Ar track
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Ar track
is
.Cm blue
or
.Cm green .
.Nm
works at two levels.
.Pp
For a workload, the demo's release has a deployment per track behind one
Service, and which track the Service selects is the switch.
.Cm cutover
refuses unless every replica of the target track is Ready, tests it, moves
the Service, and then checks that the Service's endpoints really moved \(em
what traffic will reach, not what was asked for.
.Pp
For a cluster: a CNI or Kubernetes version cannot be changed in place and
undone, so the change is made by running a second cluster beside the first
and moving to it.
Each track is a cluster of its own, named
.Ql kldload- Ns Ar track ,
cloned by
.Xr kube-cluster 8
from the same golden, with its own API address and MetalLB range so the
idle one can be tested before it is promoted.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Which track is live, and whether each is healthy.
.It Cm preview Ar track
Send real requests to the track's private address and show what comes
back, leaving production alone.
.It Cm cutover Ar track
As above.
.It Cm rollback
Cut over to the track that is not live.
.It Cm cluster status
Each track: whether it exists, whether every node is Ready, which is
active, and its kubeconfig.
.It Cm cluster deploy Ar track
Build that track's cluster; further arguments go to
.Xr kube-cluster 8 .
.It Cm cluster promote Ar track
Point
.Pa /root/.kube/config
at the track, after checking that every node is Ready, and check that it
answers.
The other track is left running.
.It Cm cluster destroy Ar track
Destroy the track, which must not be the active one.
The host's WireGuard keys and default kubeconfig, which
.Xr kube-cluster 8
removes with a cluster, are put back when another cluster is still here,
and the survivors are put on the mesh again.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RELEASE , Ev NS , Ev CHART
The workload: default
.Ql javaapi-fullstack
in namespace
.Ql demo .
.It Ev KUBECONFIG
Default
.Pa /root/.kube/config .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_BG_BLUE_VIP , Ev KLDLOAD_BG_GREEN_VIP
Each track's API address.
Blue takes
.Xr kube-cluster 8 Ns 's
own, .240; green .241.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_BG_BLUE_POOL , Ev KLDLOAD_BG_GREEN_POOL
Each track's MetalLB range: blue .200\(en.220, green .221\(en.239, on
whatever subnet
.Ql virbr0
is on.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/cluster-track
The active track.
.It Pa /root/.kube/config- Ns Ar track
Each track's kubeconfig;
.Pa /root/.kube/config
links to the active one.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when what was asked for was verified to have happened; 1 when it was
refused or could not be verified.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no cluster, on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-bluegreen cluster status

  TRACK    EXISTS     READY     ACTIVE  KUBECONFIG
  blue     no         no                /root/.kube/config-blue
  green    no         no                /root/.kube/config-green

no track is active yet — promote one to point /root/.kube/config at it
# (exited 0)
# kube-bluegreen cluster destroy purple
FATAL: unknown track 'purple'
# (exited 1)
# kube-bluegreen cluster promote green
FATAL: green has no VMs — deploy it first
# (exited 1)
# kube-bluegreen status
FATAL: release javaapi-fullstack not found in namespace demo — deploy it first
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
A cluster change; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-bluegreen cluster deploy green --workers 3
# kube-bluegreen cluster promote green
# kube-bluegreen cluster destroy blue
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-enroll 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-demo 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-21, the first time
.Cm cluster destroy
ran, it removed the host's kubeconfig and took the host off its own mesh
while another cluster on it was still running.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page, in a container:
.Cm cluster destroy
copied the host's WireGuard private keys to
.Pa /tmp
and left them there whenever the destroy failed, or the re-peer left any
machine incomplete \(em which also ended the destroy part-way.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Service addresses differ between tracks: a client that uses blue's
address is not moved by promoting green.
Handing blue's range to green at promotion is not built.
